\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds End Volatile Year In Light Trading\b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2011\par 23:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Argentine peso posts 7.6% year-on-year loss vs dollar in penultimate session of 2011\par \par \uc2 --Argentine government bonds were broadly higher this year\par \par \uc2 --Argentina's benchmark Merval index fell 30% in 2011\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Ken Parks \par    Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks and sovereign bonds posted solid gains in the last trading session of 2011, while the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closed little changed against the dollar as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept the peso steady.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Argentina's stock and bond markets are closed Friday and Monday. The MAE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wholesale market will operate until 10:30 a.m. EST Friday, and is closed Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso dominated financial headlines in the fourth quarter, after President Cristina Kirchner imposed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls in late October to limit capital flight that was slowly draining international reserves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the exchange market almost daily to engineer a gradual weakening of the peso to help exporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso was quoted closing on the MAE at ARS4.3035 to the U.S. dollar on Thursday, bringing its year-to-date loss to 7.6%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank spent billions of dollars in reserves to keep the peso steady in the run-up to October's general election, in which Kirchner won re-election by a record margin.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With a second term in her pocket, Kirchner swiftly limited the public's access to dollars by requiring all \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions be vetted by the tax agency.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors pulled more than $18 billion out of the country in the first nine months of the year on fears that annual inflation of more than 20% will eventually force authorities to weaken the peso at a faster rate to keep exports competitive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Now that private-sector dollar demand has been suffocated, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has become an active buyer of greenbacks in recent weeks. After hitting a multiyear low of $44.70 billion on Dec. 14, reserves reached $46.27 billion on Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Carlos Lizer, director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at brokerage Puente, expects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep the peso on a slow, but steady course of depreciation in the first quarter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For the end of March we expect a floor of around ARS4.40 and a ceiling of ARS4.45," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The mixed performance of Argentine stocks and government bonds this year was closely tied to international events, namely Europe's unfolding sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Events abroad will continue to drive trading in both asset classes in 2012, especially if Europe slips into recession and Argentina's top trading partners, China and Brazil, grow at a slower pace than economists currently forecast.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most benchmark bonds posted gains this year, with the notable exception of the 33% plunge in the 2033 discount bond.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, the Bonar X rose 0.7% in price terms to close at ARS407.00, yielding 8.88%. The Bogar 2018 closed 2% higher at ARS221.50, to yield 11.40%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Boden 2015 rose 1.5% to ARS449.00, yielding 6.37%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrant rose 0.8% to ARS11.54, while dollar GDP warrants closed 1.8% higher at ARS62.10.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After rallying 52% in 2010, the benchmark Merval stock index plunged 30% this year as Europe's crisis and prospects of slower global economic growth in 2012 spurred investors to exit riskier markets like Argentina.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banks and public utilities, which are heavily weighted on the index, were the biggest losers, with shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) falling 53% and electric energy holding company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pampa Energia SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (PAMP.BA, PAM) stock shedding 29% of its value.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Thursday, the Merval rose 1.5% to close at 2462.63 on volume of ARS35.8 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  recommends zero exposure to Argentine stocks, though it did note in a recent report that a rally might ensue if the government were to adopt market friendly policies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Argentina remains the only [Latin American] market that could rally driven by policy changes given: 1) significant rerating potential, and 2) many sectors are under earning under current regulatory environment," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ken Parks, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 29-12-11 2203GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111229e7ct000o3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
