\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Pension Agency Trimmed Government Bond Holdings In June\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2011\par 01:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's pension fund agency, Anses, trimmed its holdings of government securities in June compared with the previous month.\par \par \uc2 Anses's investments in public-sector debt fell 0.2% on the month to 106.5 billion pesos ($25.3 billion) at the end of June, but rose 14.2% on the year, the agency said Thursday in its monthly report on assets under management.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated Bonar X bond showed the biggest decline as a percentage of the agency's government bond portfolio, falling to 7.9% from 8.5% at the end of May. The agency's holdings of dollar-denominated Boden 2015 bonds was steady at 3.4% of the total.\par \par \uc2 Anses and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize the peso amid growing levels of capital flight in an election year.\par \par \uc2 Local traders say Anses has taken a bigger role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent months, selling and buying bonds to take some of the pressure off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has seen its reserves fall as it defends the peso.\par \par \uc2 President Cristina Kirchner is trying to avoid abrupt moves in the exchange rate that would spook voters as she seeks reelection in October. Kirchner is widely expected to win a second term after receiving just over 50% of the vote in Argentina's first open primary election in August.\par \par \uc2 But investors are speculating that Kirchner will allow the peso to depreciate at a swifter rate after the elections to help exporters, who have seen their competitiveness eroded by high inflation at home.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted closing on the local MAE \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  wholesale market at ARS4.2045 to the dollar Thursday, unchanged for the fourth straight session. The peso has depreciated about 5.4% versus the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  economist Sebastian Vargas wrote in a report Thursday that he expects Anses to play a key role in helping the government to cover an estimated financing gap of $6.4 billion in 2012.\par \par \uc2 "In its role of underwriter of treasury debt, we continue to expect Anses to tap markets for $5 billion to $6 billion in 2012," Vargas said.\par \par \uc2 The agency could sell its Bonar X positions, which totaled about ARS8.3 billion at the end of June. But the government would have to issue additional debt to Anses during the year to bridge the gap, according to \uc2 Barclays\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Anses publishes information about its investment portfolio with a three month delay to prevent market participants from speculating in Argentine assets, according to agency officials.\par \par \uc2 Anses' overall investment portfolio grew 27.2% on the year to ARS191 billion as of June 30.\par \par \uc2 The biggest gains were noted in equity investments, which rose to ARS24 billion, and financing for infrastructure and industrial projects, which totaled ARS23.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 Anses has invested in projects ranging from public housing to the completion of the Atucha II nuclear power plant as part of Kirchner's job creation policy.\par \par \uc2 Public pension systems that don't create jobs "are useless", Economy Minister and vice presidential candidate Amado Boudou said at a pension seminar earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 29-09-11 2312GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110929e79t001a8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
