\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Can Easily Manage Exchange Rate Of Peso - Official\b0\par\par\uc2 By Taos Turner   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2011\par 21:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's government can easily manage the exchange rate of the Argentine peso even if financial troubles worsen in Europe and the U.S., a top government official said in an interview this week.\par \par \uc2 "Whatever the case, whatever the situation, I don't see Argentina having any problem at all managing the exchange rate," said the official, who declined to be named. "We have enough of a cushion to keep the rate completely under control, regardless of what happens abroad."\par \par \uc2 The cushion refers to about $49.5 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves held by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses those reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying or selling dollars as needed to prevent the peso from fluctuating abruptly.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate is a particularly important variable in Argentina because of the country's history," said the official. "There's absolutely no reason for this to be an issue now or after the election in October."\par \par \uc2 Argentina holds a presidential election on Oct. 23. President Cristina Kirchner is expected to win in a landslide.\par \par \uc2 The peso currently trades for about ARS4.20 to the U.S. dollar. It has been slowly but predictably depreciating in recent years under Argentina's managed exchange-rate policy.\par \par \uc2 The peso depreciated by about 1% a month this year until August, when it weakened at an even quicker pace.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders here expect it to weaken another 10% to 11% next year, putting it at around ARS4.50.\par \par \uc2 But many economists say high inflation surpassing 20% annually is causing the peso to appreciate in real terms, crimping the competitiveness of Argentine exporters.\par \par \uc2 Some in Argentina's manufacturing sector have asked the government to let the peso slide faster. Others say letting the peso move too quickly in any direction would spook investors, especially average Argentines, who have a strong psychological aversion to a weak peso given repeated financial crises here.\par \par \uc2 "The president's job is to listen to all sectors, evaluate all the issues, and then decide to do what is best for the country as a whole. That's exactly what she's going to do," the official said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  often in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2002 economic meltdown and devaluation. Since 2003, the bank's reserves have risen from $10.5 billion, according to a report this week by the think tank Abeceb.\par \par \uc2 That trend began changing in 2008 during the global financial crisis and local political problems that spurred capital flight that reduced reserves by over 11%, Abeceb reported.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the bank also used $6.5 billion in reserves to make debt payments. This year it has used $9.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 Abeceb cautioned that using reserves too quickly could raise investor concern and lead people to buy dollars en masse.\par \par \uc2 "Though the macroeconomic situation is good, an increase in devaluation expectations could cause inflation to accelerate because a depreciating peso leads to higher prices," Abeceb said. "It would add volatility to the financial market."\par \par \uc2 -By Taos Turner, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4103-6728; taos.turner@dowjones.com [ 16-09-11 1905GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110916e79g0010l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
