\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Peso Firms On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Off\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2011\par 23:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso firmed on renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, while stocks followed U.S. markets lower after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke gave no plan for additional steps to aid the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted closing on Argentina's MAE \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  wholesale market at ARS4.2020 to the dollar, compared to ARS4.2065 at Wednesday's close.\par \par \uc2 Puente brokerage said in its afternoon note to clients that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina sold just over $60 million in dollars during the session. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , together with dollar sales by state-run banks and agro-exporters, helped to stabilize the peso just above the ARS4.20 level.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 1.5% to 2832.43 on volume of ARS48.8 million ($11.6 million).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, fell 0.7% to $12.19 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Shares of banking group \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) fell 4.6% to ARS4.77; shares of steel tube maker \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  (TS, TS.BA) lost 2.8% to close at ARS70.00; and conglomerate Sociedad Comercial del Plata SA (COME) plunged 8.4% to ARS0.73.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market totaled ARS459.7 million, accounting for about 57% of the total volume of securities traded on the exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2015 rose 0.2% in price terms to close at ARS431.50, yielding 7.30%. The Bonar X rose 0.2% to ARS400.65, yielding 8.95%.\par \par \uc2 The Bogar 2018 fell 1% in price terms to close at ARS203.51, yielding 12.96%. The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond fell 1.2% to ARS154.00, to yield 10.13%.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 08-09-11 2119GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110908e798001a4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
