\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Stocks, Bonds Slump As Wall Street Fuels Selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shane Romig   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2011\par 23:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine stocks and bonds took a beating Thursday as the sharp drop on Wall Street fueled stoked selling.\par \par \uc2 The Merval Index of leading shares slumped 1.6% to settle at 3302.44 points amid thin volume of 41 million pesos ($10 million).\par \par \uc2 Power transmitter Transener (TRAN.BA) led the losses among the Merval components, shedding 2.8% to close at ARS1.38.\par \par \uc2 In New York, stocks headed lower after Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke made comments deflating stimulus hopes in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The local stock and bond markets are taking their cues from global shifts rather than the political and economic signs back home, Estudio Ber economist Gustavo Ber said in a market note.\par \par \uc2 The exception seems to be dollar bonds, which have been enjoying support as a refuge, Ber said.\par \par \uc2 However, the sour mood on Thursday dragged down almost all bonds.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond shed 1.3% in price terms to ARS149, to yield 10.27%.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated Global 2017, fell 1.6% in price terms to ARS445, with the yield at 7.44%.\par \par \uc2 The peso eased to close at ARS4.1315 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, compared to Wednesday's close at ARS4.0978, according to \uc2 ICAP PLC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage Puente said in a note to clients that $428 million was traded over the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the session, with the peso holding steady at ARS4.1220 per dollar for a fourth straight session on the wholesale market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took advantage of grain exporters repatriating the proceeds of their sales to buy $150 million on Thursday, down from the $180 million in dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased the previous day, Puente said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased about $450 million so far this week, according to the brokerage.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure a gradual depreciation of the peso against the U.S. dollar to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6738, shane.romig@dowjones.com [ 14-07-11 2144GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110714e77e001b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
