\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks Rise On US Stimulus Talk; Merval +0.2%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2011\par 23:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks closed with modest gains on Wednesday, thanks to stronger-than-expected Chinese economic growth and comments by Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might embark on a fresh round of stimulus.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index rose 0.2% to close at 3356.44 points on volume of 49.7 million pesos ($12.1 million).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, rose 1% to close at $14.97 in New York.\par \par \uc2 U.S. and European markets got a boost after Bernanke said he would look at implementing more extraordinary stimulus measures if economic conditions worsen. Chinese data also helped local sentiment, given that China ranks as Argentina's No. 2 trading partner.\par \par \uc2 "The Merval's support level between 3320 and 3350 should hold up unless something really bad happens in global markets," said Dionisio Corneille at brokerage Corneille Agente de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 Banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) rose 0.5% to ARS6.08; mortgage bank \uc2 Banco Hipotecario SA\uc2  (BHIP.BA) rose 1.2% to ARS2.44; and oil-and-gas producer \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (YPFD.BA, YPF) recovered some of the ground lost in Tuesday's route to close 1.4% higher at ARS185.50.\par \par \uc2 Among declining issues, shares of steel maker \uc2 Siderar SAIC\uc2  (ERAR.BA) dipped 0.8% to close at ARS32.50, and shares of electric energy holding company \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAMP.BA, PAM) fell 1.2% to ARS2.58.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market totaled ARS338.4 million, equivalent to about 56% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X dipped 0.2% to end at ARS395, yielding 8.50%. The 2018 Bogar fell 0.7% to ARS205, yielding 11.92%.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 dipped 0.1% to ARS422, yielding 7.03%.\par \par \uc2 The peso firmed to close at ARS4.0978 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, compared to Tuesday's close at ARS4.1075, according to \uc2 ICAP PLC\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure a gradual depreciation of the peso against the U.S. dollar to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 13-07-11 2132GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110713e77d001be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
