\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks Rise With Global Markets; Merval Gains 0.7%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2011\par 23:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks closed higher Thursday as investors cheered a better-than-expected jobs report in the U.S. and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to suspend collateral rules on Portugal's debt.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index rose 0.7% to close at 3487.21 points on volume of 59.7 million pesos ($14.6 million).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, rose 1.3% to close at $15.44 in New York.\par \par \uc2 U.S. markets closed firmly higher, as did most major European indexes, after a better-than-expected measure of private-sector hiring in the U.S. raised hopes that the world's largest economy is on the mend.\par \par \uc2 "All in all, there is a better tone in the market. Fears that we are in for more declines seem to have dissipated," said a Buenos Aires-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) rose 1.8% to ARS6.16; electric energy holding company \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAM, PAMP.BA) rose 2.3% to ARS2.73; and diversified industrial conglomerate Ledesma SA (LEDE.BA) rose 2.4% to ARS9.06.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS378.9 million, equivalent to about 50% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated warrants of gross domestic product fell 0.4% to close at ARS16.80, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity closed 0.1% lower at ARS76.50.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X dipped 0.2% to ARS397.25, to yield 8.32%. The Bocon 2024 bond fell 0.6% to ARS109.05, yielding 12.47%.\par \par \uc2 The peso firmed to close at ARS4.1031 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, compared to Wednesday's close at ARS4.1060, according to \uc2 ICAP PLC\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure a gradual depreciation of the peso against the U.S. dollar to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 07-07-11 2145GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110707e7770019z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
