\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds Rise On Greece Bailout; Merval +0.8%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2011\par 23:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine stocks and bonds rose on Wednesday, after Greece managed to avoid a near-term default by approving a harsh austerity plan demanded by the European Union and International Monetary Fund in exchange for financial aid.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index rose 0.8% to close at 3353.82 points on volume of 48.3 million pesos ($11.8 million).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, rose 1% to close at $14.77 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Global stock markets closed sharply higher on Wednesday after Greece's parliament approved the 5-year austerity package. Investors feared that failure to pass the measures would have forced Greece to default, potentially triggering a new international financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 A Buenos Aires-based trader said positive momentum from U.S. and European markets spilled over into Argentina during the session.\par \par \uc2 "The [local] market will continue to move with international events," he said.\par \par \uc2 Banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) rose 0.2% to ARS5.74; bank \uc2 Banco Macro SA\uc2  (BMA.BA, BMA) closed 2.6% higher at ARS15.95; aluminium maker \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA, AAARF) rose 0.6% to ARS4.87; and electricity distribution firm \uc2 Edenor SA\uc2  (EDN.BA, EDN) rose 1% to ARS2.11.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS485.1 million, equivalent to about 69% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants rose 1% to close at ARS16.49, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity rose 1.2% to ARS73.60.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X dipped 0.1% to ARS387.25, to yield 8.78%. The 2018 Bogar rose 0.9% to ARS209, yielding 10.86%.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2038 Par bond closed 3.5% higher at ARS58.00 to yield 8.61%. The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 rose 0.2% to ARS416.50, yielding 7.21%.\par \par \uc2 The peso eased to close at ARS4.1073 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, compared to Tuesday's close at ARS4.0999, according to \uc2 ICAP Plc\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure a gradual depreciation of the peso against the U.S. dollar to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage firm Puente said in its afternoon comment that $400 million changed hands on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling $65 million to stabilize the peso amid heavy demand for the dollar by the private sector.\par \par \uc2 "As usually happens at this time of the month, a lot of sales aren't reflected [on the market] because the intermediaries charged with selling those dollars opt to hold onto them to be positioned in dollars at the end of the month," Puente strategists wrote.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 29-06-11 2107GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110629e76t0019g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
