\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks Decline After S&P Cuts Greece; Merval -0.8%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks and Taos Turner   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2011\par 23:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine stocks closed lower Monday after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgraded Greece's sovereign credit rating, curbing investor appetitive for riskier emerging-market assets.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 0.8% to 3202.28 points in very low volume of 26.6 million pesos ($6.5 million) changing hands during the session.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, slipped 0.8% to close at $14.11 in New York.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., major stock indexes closed largely unchanged as worries over Greece's public debt overshadowed a fresh round of mergers and acquisitions.\par \par \uc2 What is happening in Argentina "is very tied to what's happening on Wall Street," said Horacio Corneille, a trader at a brokerage carrying his family name.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Corneille said, local money-laundering rules have made it harder to trade and are keeping volume low.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are thinking 30 times before putting up money now," he said, citing the bureaucratic nature of the rules.\par \par \uc2 He also said uncertainty about October's presidential election is keeping investors on the sidelines. So far, President Cristina Fernandez has yet to say if she will run. "Moreover, it's unclear what the opposition will do," Corneille said.\par \par \uc2 Banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) fell 1.1% to ARS5.30, electric utility holding \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAMP.BA) closed 1.1% lower at ARS2.62, and oil company \uc2 Petrobras Argentina SA\uc2  (PESA.BA, PZE) fell 2.5% to ARS7.90.\par \par \uc2 Local bank \uc2 Banco Macro SA\uc2  (BMA.BA, BMA) bucked the trend, with its shares rising 2.1% to ARS14.60.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants rose 0.12% to ARS16.25, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity fell 0.14% to ARS73.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 fell 0.14% to ARS422, yielding 6.6%.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters as unchanged at ARS4.0925 versus the U.S. dollar on interbank markets.\par \par \uc2 Though the market cost of a dollar was unchanged, the cost of physical bills in informal markets rose half a centavo because of delays in the importation of dollar bills.\par \par \uc2 Flights in and out of Argentina recently have been canceled because of ash clouds related to volcanic activity in Chile. This has delayed the delivery of dollars that normally would have arrived on those flights, the local brokerage Puente said Monday in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure a gradual depreciation of the peso against the U.S. dollar to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 13-06-11 2147GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110613e76d0012w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
