\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Argentina's Alfonsin To Focus On Inflation, Peso If Elected - Adviser\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alberto Messer and Taos Turner  \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2011\par 21:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's leading opposition presidential candidate, Ricardo Alfonsin, would focus on fighting double-digit inflation and preventing the peso from appreciating if elected, a top adviser said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is creating a lot of problems," Adrian Ramos, Alfonsin's chief economic adviser, said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Alfonsin would use a "multiple anchor strategy" to gradually reduce inflation through a combination of fiscal, monetary and tax policies, he said.\par \par \uc2 Argentina holds presidential and congressional elections Oct. 23. Alfonsin, a congressman from the Union Civica Radical party, is likely to be the top challenger to incumbent President Cristina Fernandez, if she runs.\par \par \uc2 Ramos said inflation is pummeling the poor and making it hard for investors to make long-term decisions. He also described the peso's inflation-adjusted appreciation as "unsustainable."\par \par \uc2 To help local exporters, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to gradually weaken the peso against the U.S. dollar. So far this year, the peso has lost about 2.8% versus the dollar, following a 4.5% slide last year. But this nominal depreciation contrasts with annual inflation that most economists say is well above 20%.\par \par \uc2 Soaring inflation and the crawling depreciation have led to a de facto 15% appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ramos said.\par \par \uc2 The peso was recently quoted by Thomson Reuters as trading at ARS4.0925 to the dollar on interbank markets.\par \par \uc2 Ramos said tackling inflation would require restoring credibility at the national statistics agency, Indec.\par \par \uc2 The veracity of Indec's data has been questioned ever since President Fernandez's husband and predecessor, Nestor Kirchner, reorganized the agency in early 2007.\par \par \uc2 Kirchner replaced many civil servants with political appointees and Indec's statistics soon began diverging from private-sector estimates, leading analysts to conclude that Indec manipulates economic data for ulterior motives.\par \par \uc2 Indec officials have repeatedly denied the charges.\par \par \uc2 Ramos said another Alfonsin priority would be ensuring that Argentina has access to global capital markets.\par \par \uc2 "We won't necessarily tap capital markets, but apart from the actual decision to issue debt, we need to have the ability to do so," he said.\par \par \uc2 Ramos indicated Alfonsin might also use the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves to make debt payments.\par \par \uc2 "There's no written dogma saying that they can't be used," Ramos said. "But it depends on the circumstances. If it's done because public accounts are in a complicated situation, that pushes the interest rate up. In that case, using reserves is not a good strategy because it creates more uncertainty."\par \par \uc2 Ramos also said Alfonsin would likely cut taxes on beef, wheat and other farm exports.\par \par \uc2 "The sector is demanding changes in these policies and we think it's important to do it," he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Taos Turner, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4103-6728; taos.turner@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 09, 2011 15:11 ET (19:11 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110609e7690059i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
