\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds Rebound With Wall Street; Merval +3.5%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2011\par 23:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks rallied and bonds logged modest gains on Thursday, as buyers waded back into the local market following two weeks of heavy selling.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index rose 3.5% to 3232.86 points with 68.4 million pesos ($16.7 million) changing hands during the session. Thursday's rally was the Merval's biggest one-day gain since last November and brought the index's year-to-date losses to 8.3%.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, rose 1.6% to $14.34 in New York.\par \par \uc2 In the U.S., the Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 0.6% and the broader S&P 500 index closed up 0.7% as bargain hunters snapped up stocks beaten down by six consecutive losing sessions. European markets closed firmly higher.\par \par \uc2 "Today we rebounded strongly with the U.S. As long as there is nothing hugely negative abroad this recovery might have legs," said Diego Zavaleta, head trader at Buenos Aires-based Besfamille Sociedad de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 Banks fronted gains on the Merval during the session, with \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.GA, GGAL) up 4.5% to ARS5.32, cross-town rival \uc2 BBVA Banco Frances SA\uc2  (FRAN.BA, BFR) up 4.3% to ARS13.35, and \uc2 Banco Macro SA\uc2  (BMA.BA, BMA) gaining 3.3% to close at ARS14.10.\par \par \uc2 Shares of electric utility holding \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAMP.BA, PAM) jumped 6.5% to ARS2.64. Pampa's electricity distribution subsidiary \uc2 Edenor SA\uc2  (EDN.BA, EDN) jumped 10% to ARS1.98, and transmission unit Transener SA (TRAN.BA) closed 12.5% higher at ARS1.35.\par \par \uc2 Industrial stocks also did well, with \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA) up 1.6% to ARS4.60, and Ledesma SA (LEDE.BA) rising 6.7% to ARS8.55.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS524.8 million, equivalent to about 57% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants fell 0.3% to ARS16.25, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity rose 0.6% to close at ARS74.45.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X rose 0.4% to ARS396.40, to yield 8.08%. The 2018 Bogar closed 0.2% higher at ARS208, yielding 11%.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 rose 0.4%, to close at ARS422.50, yielding 6.61%.\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage Puente said in a report that medium-duration government bonds liked the Boden 2015, Bonar 2017 and Global 2017 are a good investment opportunity.\par \par \uc2 "We see value in those three alternatives, preferably the Bonar 2017, which has an attractive yield," Puente analysts wrote.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters as finishing unchanged from Wednesday's close at ARS4.0925 versus the U.S. dollar on interbank markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure a gradual depreciation of the peso against the U.S. dollar to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 Puente said that volume on the local exchange market was about $453 million during the session, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying about $60 million.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 09-06-11 2127GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110609e769001al\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
