\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks Close Higher With Wall Street; Merval +0.2%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2011\par 23:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks recovered from early losses to close with modest gains on Thursday, tracking a rebound in U.S. markets.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index rose nearly 0.2%, to close at 3389.73 on volume of 50.6 million pesos ($12.4 million).\par \par \uc2 However, the \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks the shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, fell 1.4%, to close at US$14.79 in New York.\par \par \uc2 U.S. markets reversed steep morning losses to close higher, led by gains in defensive stocks in the consumer staples and health care sectors. A jump in commodities prices also helped buoy investor sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL, GGAL.BA) rose 0.7%, to ARS5.74; electricity distribution company \uc2 Edenor SA\uc2  (EDN, EDN.BA) rose nearly 1%, to ARS2.08; and aluminium maker \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA) closed 1.7% higher, at ARS5.37.\par \par \uc2 Among declining issues, the shares of oil companies \uc2 Petrobras Argentina SA\uc2  (PZE, PESA.BA) fell 2.5%, to ARS9.10, and \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (YPF, YPFD.BA) closed 1.1% lower, at ARS190.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS669.2 million, equivalent to 83% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants closed unchanged at ARS16.8750, while U.S. dollar-denominated warrants with the same maturity rose 0.4%, to close at ARS74.7990.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X rose 0.8%, to ARS398.50, to yield 7.79%. The 2018 Bogar rose 0.6%, to ARS206.25, yielding 10.91%.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond closed 2.5% higher, at ARS156.75, to yield 9.48%. The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 rose 0.5%, to ARS423, yielding 6.39%.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters closing at ARS4.0825 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, slightly weaker than Wednesday's ARS4.0850 close.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with a bias toward a gradual depreciation to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 12-05-11 2146GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110512e75c001xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
