\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Stocks, Bonds Rise After US Jobs Report; Merval +0.3%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2011\par 23:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks pared their early gains to close modestly higher Friday, led by financial and industrial shares as markets cautiously cheered a better-than-expected U.S. jobs report.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index rose 0.3% to close at 3315.84 on volume of 44.7 million pesos ($11 million). Even so, the Merval fell 2.7% for the week, bringing its year-to-date loss to 5.9%.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks the shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, rose 0.7% to close at US$14.72 in New York.\par \par \uc2 U.S. markets closed in the black, though well off their intraday highs, after the government reported a 244,000 gain in jobs last month, handily beating analysts' expectations. The unemployment rate, however, rose to 9% from 8.8% in March.\par \par \uc2 Next week, investor attention will likely remain riveted on first-quarter corporate earnings and international events, including U.S. economic data and Europe's simmering debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 "Earnings are expected to be good, especially at banks which are going to stand out thanks to strong growth in credit to the private sector," said a Buenos Aires-based trader.\par \par \uc2 Shares of steel tube maker \uc2 Tenaris SA\uc2  (TS, TS.BA) rose 2.7% to ARS103.50. On Thursday, the company reported a 46% increase in first-quarter net profit and said global oil and gas drilling activity will grow through the year.\par \par \uc2 Banking group \uc2 Banco Macro SA\uc2  (BMA, BMA.BA) rose 1.3% to ARS15.25; aluminum maker \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA) climbed 0.6% to ARS5.18; and shares of phone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina SA\uc2  (TEO, TECO2.BA) rose 0.5% to ARS20.35.\par \par \uc2 Among declining issues, shares of electric utility \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAM, PAMP.BA) slipped 0.8% to close at ARS2.52, while shares of steel maker \uc2 Siderar SAIC\uc2  (ERAR.BA) fell 0.5% to ARS31.85.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's securities regulator, the CNV, on Friday lifted the trading ban on Siderar's shares after the company said it won't make an upcoming dividend payment due to a legal battle with the government.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the CNV ordered Siderar to hold a new shareholders meeting within the next 10 days after the regulator voided the annual general shareholders meeting held on April 15 due to "irregularities."\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS426.1 million, equivalent to nearly 78% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants rose 0.3% to ARS17.06, while U.S. dollar-denominated warrants with the same maturity rose 0.6% to close at ARS73.45.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X rose 1.1% to ARS391.50, to yield 8.13%. The 2018 Bogar fell 0.2% to ARS209.50, yielding 10.34%.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond closed 1% higher at ARS159.50, to yield 9.29%. The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 rose 0.8% to ARS413.40, yielding 6.97%.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters closing at ARS4.0825 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, slightly weaker than Thursday's ARS4.0800 close.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with a bias toward a gradual depreciation to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 06-05-11 2116GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110506e756001hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
