\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks Dip On Weak US Data; Merval -0.7%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2011\par 23:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks closed in the red on Wednesday, led by declines in energy and industrial shares following disappointing data for the U.S. service sector and labor market.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 0.7% to close at 3352.22 on volume of 45.3 million pesos ($11.1 million).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks the shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, fell 1.4% to close at US$14.78 in New York.\par \par \uc2 U.S. markets closed firmly lower in the wake of private-sector reports that showed a dramatic slowdown in the service sector and job creation in April that fell short of economists' expectations.\par \par \uc2 "The volume in Argentina's market today was small. We're facing an uphill battle as the government tries to gain power in more private-sector companies. That is leading to more caution in the market and putting investors on the sidelines. We've had some good earnings reports, but this battle between the government and the companies is holding investors back," said Dionisio Corneille, a trader at a Buenos Aires-based brokerage that carries his family name.\par \par \uc2 Shares of oil company \uc2 Petrobras Argentina SA\uc2  (PESA.BA, PZE) plunged 4.6% to ARS9.02; shares of aluminum maker \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA) fell 1.9% to ARS5.22; shares of electric utility \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAM, PAMP.BA) slipped 1.1% to close at ARS2.61.\par \par \uc2 Among gaining issues, shares of the country's largest oil and gas producer, \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (YPFD.BA, YPF), rose 0.3% to finish at ARS177.\par \par \uc2 Spanish oil major \uc2 Repsol YPF SA\uc2  (REP.MI) said Wednesday that Argentina's \uc2 Grupo Petersen\uc2  has exercised an option to buy an additional 10% stake in its YPF unit for $1.3 billion.\par \par \uc2 The transaction will be completed in the "next few days" and will see \uc2 Grupo Petersen\uc2 's stake in Argentina's No. 1 oil and gas producer rise to 25.46%. Once the deal closes, \uc2 Repsol YPF\uc2  will still hold a 58.23% controlling interest in YPF.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS477.3 million, equivalent to 52% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 U.S. dollar-denominated gross domestic product warrants fell 0.6% to close at ARS73.80.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X rose 0.2% to ARS387.60, to yield 8.34%. The 2018 Bogar fell 0.4% to ARS213.25, yielding 9.73%.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond fell 1.8% to ARS161, to yield 9.19%. The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 rose 0.2% to ARS409, yielding 7.25%.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters as closing unchanged from Tuesday's finish at ARS4.0800 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with a bias toward a gradual depreciation to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 04-05-11 2122GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110504e754001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
