\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks Dip, Bonds Are Mixed; Eyes On US Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2011\par 23:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks closed lower while bonds were mixed on Monday, as the local market searched for direction with major U.S. indexes posting modest losses ahead of a slew of economic data later in the week.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 0.3% to close at 3395.64 on volume of 32.1 million pesos ($7.9 million).\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks opened higher after the U.S. confirmed that it had killed Osama bin Laden in Pakistan, but that initial euphoria dissipated as the session wore on and investors shifted their focus to economic data and corporate earnings. Friday's key employment report will be closely watched for clues about the health of the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 "The [local] market has been fairly erratic in terms of establishing a trend, with investors following events abroad. There is a lot of apathy on the market and volumes are low," a Buenos Aires-based trader said.\par \par \uc2 Banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL.BA, GGAL) dipped 0.2% to close at ARS5.47; telephone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina SA\uc2  (TECO2.BA, TEO) fell 1.6% to ARS19.10; and electric utility \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAM, PAMP.BA) rose 2.3% to close at ARS2.66.\par \par \uc2 The Buenos Aires Stock Exchange suspended trading in the shares of steel company \uc2 Siderar SAIC\uc2  (ERAR.BA, SDDFF) on Monday in response to the company's decision Friday to proceed with plans to pay dividends totaling ARS1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 At its annual general shareholders' meeting April 15, Siderar approved the dividend payment, but last week a judge issued an injunction against the payment after the government asked courts to void the shareholders' meeting.\par \par \uc2 Pension agency Anses has attempted to gain greater influence at Siderar by placing a representative of its choice on the company's board of directors in virtue of the 26% stake it owns in the steel maker. Siderar is fighting Anses's demands for board representation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks the shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, fell 1% to close at US$15.21 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS371.4 million, equivalent to 44% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 U.S. dollar-denominated gross domestic product warrants rose 1.2% to close at ARS74.40.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar-denominated 2017 Bonar X closed 0.2% lower at ARS386.10, to yield 8.41%. The 2018 Bogar fell 1.4% to ARS212, pushing the yield up to 9.89%.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond rose 0.9% to ARS163, to yield 9.06%. The U.S. dollar-denominated Boden 2015 fell 0.2% to close at ARS407.25, yielding 7.35%.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters as closing unchanged from last Friday's close at ARS4.0800 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with a bias toward a gradual depreciation to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 02-05-11 2106GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110502e752000yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgo