\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds Slip On Weak Volume; Merval -0.9%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2011\par 23:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks finished lower in slack trading Monday, as investors showed little appetite for stocks ahead of the start of first-quarter earnings season in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 0.9% to close at 3448.12 points on volume of 30.2 million pesos ($7.5 million).\par \par \uc2 "In this market you have to move fast; buy what drops a lot and sell what rises a lot. It's a trading market," Agusto Farina, an equity trader at local brokerage Amirante Galitis, said in reference to the local stock market.\par \par \uc2 Shares of banking group \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL, GGAL.BA) fell 1.6% to close at ARS5.71; shares of electric utility holding company \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAMP.BA, PAM) fell 2% to ARS2.43; and shares of phone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina\uc2  (TEO, TECO2.BA) slipped 0.2% to ARS21.30.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks the shares of Argentine companies listed on international markets, fell 1.4% to $15.50 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS497.4 million, equivalent to 54% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The Bogar 2018 closed 0.1% lower at ARS223.75, yielding 7.88%. The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond slipped 0.1% to ARS173, to yield 8.34%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants rose 0.1% to ARS17.41, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity fell 0.8% to ARS72.9450.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters closing at ARS4.0525 to the dollar on interbank markets, unchanged from Friday's close.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with a depreciating bias.\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage Puente said in its afternoon note to clients that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated $100 million on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "The daily purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market, and occasionally the futures market, show its willingness to keep the U.S. dollar-peso exchange rate above ARS4.05 by giving [grains exporters] a floor at which to sell their dollar holdings while at the same time restocking foreign reserves," Puente said.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 11-04-11 2101GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110411e74b001ay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
