\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Markets Slump As Fears Over Japan Spark Selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shane Romig   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine bond and stock markets posted steep declines Tuesday as the problems in Japan fuelled a selloff across global markets.\par \par \uc2 The Merval Index of leading shares ended the day 2.8% lower at ARS3,263.27. Volume was relatively heavy at ARS105 million ($26 million).\par \par \uc2 Argentine markets faced sharp selling pressure from the opening bell after Asian and European markets slumped following a warning from Japan's prime minister of substantial radiation leaks at a damaged nuclear-power plant. Japan's Nikkei Stock Average fell 11% and sent major European indexes to 2011 lows.\par \par \uc2 While Argentina and Japan have limited trade links, the flight from risk weighed on Argentine assets throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Shares of the country's largest oil and gas producer \uc2 YPF SA\uc2  (YPFD.BA, YPF)posted the sharpest losses among the index leaders Tuesday, falling 7% to settle at ARS199.\par \par \uc2 YPF shares were stung by falling oil prices and Monday's decision by controlling shareholder \uc2 Repsol YPF\uc2  (REP.MC) to sell up to 7.1% of the Argentine company through American Depositary Shares.\par \par \uc2 Power distributer Transener (TRAN.BA) also underperformed the market, shedding 5.6% to close at ARS1.35.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Global X FTSE Argentina 20 ETF\uc2 , which tracks the globally listed shares of Argentine companies, fell 1.75% to close at $14.41 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Argentine bonds also slumped as investors shied away from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bonds fell down 1.3% at ARS158, yielding 9.18%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 dollar-denominated GDP warrants fell 1.3% to close at ARS63.30.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters closing at ARS4.0350 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, slightly weaker than the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ARS4.0300 close on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the dollar, but with a bias towards a gradual depreciation to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6738; shane.romig@dowjones.com [ 15-03-11 2137GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110315e73f001j5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
