\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds Finish Lower In Light Trading\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks closed in the red for a fourth consecutive session on Friday, as lingering fears about civil unrest in the Middle East and north Africa, along with Europe's sovereign debt crisis, offset a rally in the U.S. and neighboring Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 2.41 points to close at 3,403.51 on volume of 47.3 million pesos ($11.7 million). The Merval lost 1.9% in a holiday-shortened trading week with local financial markets closed on Monday and Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks rallied as investors bet corporations stand to benefit from rebuilding efforts in Japan, which suffered a devastating earthquake Friday that caused widespread damage along the country's northeast coast. However, civil war in Libya and protests in oil-rich Saudi Arabia weighed on investor sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Agusto Farina, an equity trader at Buenos Aires-based brokerage Amirante Galitis, said local stock market will probably be characterized by volatility and greater trading volumes next week.\par \par \uc2 "We are going to be influenced by what happens abroad," said Farina, who thinks investors will focus on events in Libya and the risk of further sovereign credit rating downgrades in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Shares of electric distribution firm \uc2 Edenor SA\uc2  (EDN, EDN.BA) rose 3.6% to ARS2.28; shares of banking firm \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL, GGAL.BA) fell 0.2% to ARS5.90; shares of \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA) dipped 0.7% to close at ARS5.63; and shares of diversified manufacturer and sugar producer Ledesma SA (LEDE.BA) rose 2.1% to ARS9.14.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS488.6 million, equivalent to 72% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond fell 2.8% to ARS162.25, yielding 8.91%. The 2018 Bogar lost 2.4% to close at ARS215.50, yielding 8.76%.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters closing at ARS4.0300 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, slightly stronger than the ARS4.0325 close on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but with a bias towards a gradual depreciation to help exporters.\par \par \uc2 Local brokerage Puente said in its afternoon \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  comment that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably bought between $120 million and $150 million of dollars during the session.\par \par \uc2 "Even though it was the biggest purchase during a session so far in March, [the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] couldn't prevent the exchange rate from firming," Puente \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 11-03-11 2159GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110311e73b001i9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
