\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Stocks, Bonds Track Global Market Gains; Merval +1.2%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2011\par 23:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks and bonds closed higher Tuesday, as local assets tracked a rally in international markets following upbeat economic data pointing to a broad recovery in the global economy.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval index rose 1.2% to close at 3635.26 points on volume of 44.5 million pesos ($11.1 million). The index is up 3.2% so far this year, after rising nearly 2% in January.\par \par \uc2 U.S. equity markets rallied Tuesday following better-than-expected manufacturing data. European stock markets also logged gains following a survey showing that euro-zone manufacturing activity accelerated at its fastest pace in nine months.\par \par \uc2 Aluminium maker \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  SA (ALUA.BA) rose 2.6% to ARS6.01, phone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina\uc2  (TEO, TECO2.BA) rose 2.6% to ARS21.70, and electricity transmission firm Transener SA (TRAN.BA) closed 3.1% higher at ARS1.69.\par \par \uc2 Among declining issues, shares of grain exporter \uc2 Molinos Rio de la Plata SA\uc2  (MOLI.BA) fell 1.4% to ARS37.00. Molinos is one of several grain exporters and edible oil makers whose \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been disrupted by striking workers that have blocked access to key ports along the Parana River.\par \par \uc2 Turnover on the local bond market was ARS306.1 billion, equivalent to 54.8% of the total volume of securities traded on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange during the session.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond rose 0.8% to ARS183.50, yielding 7.59%. The Boden 2015 rose 1.4% to ARS391.75, yielding 8.41%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants closed 1.3% higher at ARS15.44, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity rose 1.3% to ARS63.60.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted by Thomson Reuters closing at ARS4.0100 to the U.S. dollar on interbank markets, compared with ARS4.0080 at Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight band relative to the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 01-02-11 2209GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110201e721001gh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
