\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Stocks, Bonds Finish Lower On European Debt Doubts\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2010\par 22:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks and bonds closed lower Monday, amid broad declines in global markets as investors found little solace in Ireland's financial-aid package.\par \par \uc2 European markets tumbled as investors feared that the European Union's bailout of Ireland won't stop other heavily indebted countries in the union from seeking a rescue. Meanwhile, U.S. markets tempered their losses in a late-session bounce.\par \par \uc2 Turnover in the local bond market totaled 597.3 billion pesos ($150 million), accounting for 79% of the overall volume on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange.\par \par \uc2 The peso-denominated 2033 discount bond closed 0.6% lower at ARS186, yielding 7.09%. The Bogar 18 fell nearly 1% to close at ARS229, yielding 5.62%.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2015, considered a good proxy for measuring the appeal of newly issued government bonds or the government's ability to sell them, fell 1.9% to ARS368.70, yielding 9.46%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants fell 1.8% to ARS13.00, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity closed 4.6% lower at ARS53.90.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted in interbank markets closing at ARS3.9850 to the U.S. dollar, slightly weaker from the ARS3.9825 at Friday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading in a tight range against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 1% to close at 3270.10 points. Volume was nearly ARS60 million.\par \par \uc2 Electric utility holding company \uc2 Pampa Energia\uc2  (PAM, PAMP.BA) fell 2.1% to ARS2.76, banking group Grupo Financiero Galicia (GGAL, GGAL.BA) closed 1% lower at ARS6.22, and shares of phone company \uc2 Telecom Argentina\uc2  (TEO, TECO2.BA) tumbled 3% to ARS19.40.\par \par \uc2 The BNY Mellon Argentina ADR Index, which tracks U.S.-listed shares of Argentine stocks, fell 0.5% to 281.09.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740; ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 29-11-10 2126GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101129e6bt001g5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
