\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Stocks, Bonds Plunge On Global Selloff; Merval -4.2%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2010\par 19:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's stocks and bonds slumped Tuesday afternoon, as fears of higher interest rates in China and renewed sovereign debt problems in the euro zone sparked heavy selling in global markets.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index was off 4.2% at 3,132.62 points around 1:36 p.m. EST, led by declines in bank shares. Volume was 81.3 million pesos ($20.5 million).\par \par \uc2 Mortgage lender \uc2 Banco Hipotecario SA\uc2  (BHIP.BA) was off 3.8% at ARS3.07; banking concern BBVA Banco Frances (BFR, FRAN.BA) was 5.2% lower at ARS15.65, and cross-town rival Grupo Financiero Galicia (GGAL, GGAL.BA) was down 5.8% at ARS5.88.\par \par \uc2 Among industrial issues, shares of aluminium maker \uc2 Aluar Aluminio Argentino\uc2  (ALUA.BA) were trading 3% lower at ARS5.17, while shares of electric utility holding company \uc2 Pampa Energia\uc2  (PAM, PAMP.BA) were down 3.1% at ARS2.19.\par \par \uc2 The BNY Mellon Argentina ADR Index, which tracks U.S.-listed shares of Argentine stocks, was down 4.1% at 263.98.\par \par \uc2 The peso was quoted in interbank markets trading at ARS3.9725 to the U.S. dollar, unchanged from Monday's close. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to keep the peso trading within a tight range against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 On the local bond market, the federal government's benchmark peso-denominated 2033 discount bond was down 2.8% in price to trade at ARS170.15, yielding 7.95%.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2015, considered a good proxy for measuring the appeal of newly issued government bonds or the government's ability to sell them, was 1.6% lower at ARS364.75, yielding 9.59%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants were off 2.4% at ARS12.60, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity fell 3.4% to ARS52.3480.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 16-11-10 1853GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101116e6bg001cc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
