\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina's Bonds Extend Gains, Stocks Fall Led By Galicia\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ken Parks   \par \uc2 OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2010\par 00:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentina's bonds extended their gains on Thursday as global investors continued to favor high-yielding emerging market debt, while stocks fell for a second-straight session led by declines in banking concern \uc2 Grupo Financiero Galicia SA\uc2  (GGAL).\par \par \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  said in a report Thursday that lower grade external debt should benefit as an increasing number of central banks in developing countries implement capital controls and other measures aimed at stemming the appreciation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We see this as a potentially favourable development for Argentine external debt," RBC Capital strategists wrote.\par \par \uc2 The federal government's benchmark peso-denominated 2033 discount bond closed 0.5% higher in price terms at ARS155.50, yielding 8.82%.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2015, considered a good proxy for measuring the appeal of newly issued government bonds or the government's ability to sell them, rose 0.3% to close at ARS362.40, yielding 9.44%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Global 2017 bond, issued in June as part of the government's debt swap with the holders of defaulted bonds, rose 0.2% to close at ARS401.75, yielding 9.31%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's 2035 peso-denominated GDP warrants dipped 0.4% to finish at ARS11.45, while U.S. dollar-denominated GDP warrants with the same maturity fell 0.7% to ARS48.50.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed unchanged at ARS3.96 to the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the peso within a tight band.\par \par \uc2 While the majority of Latin American central banks have only had limited success in keeping their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from firming, \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  said the possibility that they succeed in weakening their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could put pressure on Argentina to do the same.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the most relevant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to track is [the Brazilian real], given competing manufacturing sectors, particularly in the automotive sphere," it said.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Merval stock index fell 0.8% to close at 2641.40. Volume in the stock market was ARS88.1 million ($22.2 million).\par \par \uc2 Shares of Galicia fell 2% to ARS3.91; shares of telephone giant \uc2 Telecom Argentina SA\uc2  (TECO2.BA, TEO) closed 1.7% lower at ARS17.05; and shares of energy holding company \uc2 Pampa Energia SA\uc2  (PAMP.BA) closed 0.6% higher at ARS1.79.\par \par \uc2 -By Ken Parks, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6740, ken.parks@dowjones.com [ 07-10-10 2200GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101007e6a7001i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
