\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Inflation casts cloud over modest Argentine rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 980 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2010\par 18:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Inflation expected to speed to 20 pct as growth picks up\par \par \uc2 * Central banker seen backing state spending, depreciation\par \par \uc2 * Price rises hit president's support base hardest\par \par \uc2 By Helen Popper\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Feb 10 (Reuters) - Argentines may have tolerated inflation of 20 percent when the economy was booming, but with only modest growth seen this year, rising prices look set to aggravate President Cristina Fernandez's economic woes.\par \par \uc2 In a nation of steak lovers, the surge in beef prices is making headlines and economic analysts are warning of a more generalized spike in inflation. Any such spike will likely fuel pay rise demands and take its toll on Fernandez's support base among the poor.\par \par \uc2 Her appointment of a pro-government economist, Mercedes Marco del Pont, to head the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month suggests Fernandez is determined to press on with expansionist policies whatever the inflationary cost.\par \par \uc2 "We've left the wolf to look after the sheep. (Marco del Pont) talks about devaluing the peso, increasing the money supply and she has played down the inflationary problem ... it sends a horrible message," said Nicolas Salvatore, an economist from the University of Buenos Aires.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts fear a weaker peso <ARSB=> and cheaper credit would make for an inflationary cocktail in Latin America's No. 3 economy, where prices rose by an estimated 15 percent in 2009 even as the economy slowed following a six-year boom.\par \par \uc2 Most private surveys expect a tentative recovery of 3 percent or 4 percent growth this year to be accompanied by inflation of about 20 percent.\par \par \uc2 INDEC, the official statistics bureau which is widely seen as underreporting inflation over the past three years, said prices rose 7.7 percent last year.\par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Amado Boudou has dismissed the surge in steak prices as "an adjustment of relative prices," saying livestock shortages were due to recent rains that meant ranchers were leaving animals out to graze. For full story, see[ID:nN02139634]\par \par \uc2 "I don't see an inflationary process in Argentina," he told the Pagina12 daily in an interview on Monday.\par \par \uc2 But powerful trade union leader Hugo Moyano, a close government ally, said inflation is "a reality no one can deny," raising the specter of tensions over consumer prices.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Marco del Pont replaces former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Martin Redrado, who Fernandez sacked earlier this month because he opposed her plan to use $6.6 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to help pay this year's rising debt obligations.\par \par \uc2 The plan, which critics called inflationary because it would have let the government maintain high levels of public spending, was blocked by the courts. But the government is lobbying to resuscitate the plan by winning support in Congress. [ID:nN08146410]\par \par \uc2 With a close ally installed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Fernandez may be able to tap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves after all, which would further increase the money supply.\par \par \uc2 If former \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Martin Redrado did little to stem soaring prices -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not set a benchmark lending rate or an inflation target range -- Marco del Pont will do even less as she focuses on boosting growth.\par \par \uc2 "It's likely that the new authorities will focus on a vigorous increase in private credit," Buenos Aires-based consulting firm Prefinex said in a report, adding that it expected government pressure on banks to lend and fewer sales of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notes and bills that absorb peso liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Marco del Pont is expected to continue Argentina's long-time policy of maintaining a relatively weak peso <ARSB=> through daily \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports competitive.\par \par \uc2 January's inflation data is due to be reported on Friday, and analysts expect the official data to only partially reflect a jump in food and drink prices and in tourism expenses over the Southern Hemisphere summer holidays.\par \par \uc2 Observers also say an acceleration in inflation will make it harder for Boudou to pursue his effort to restore credibility to the INDEC data by gradually narrowing the gap between official figures and private price surveys.\par \par \uc2 "The only thing an acceleration in inflation will do is widen the gap that was narrowed last year ... and prolong the distortion," said Gabriel Martini, an economist at Buenos Aires consultancy Abeceb.com.\par \par \uc2 WAGE DEMANDS\par \par \uc2 Any surge in inflation will pile pressure on the president to hike public-sector wages, pensions and welfare payments at a time when she can ill afford to.\par \par \uc2 Fernandez faces a widening fiscal deficit and debt repayments of some $15 billion this year -- up to $7 billion of which must still be funded. She will be loath to cut spending in the run-up to a presidential vote next year.\par \par \uc2 Her approval ratings have dropped to about 20 percent and support for her administration remains strongest among the poor, who are hardest hit by rises in food and drinks prices, which INDEC said climbed 1.6 percent in December.\par \par \uc2 Rather than sacrifice growth, Fernandez is more likely to resort to the unorthodox price controls, subsidies and export curbs used to tame prices in recent years.\par \par \uc2 But with her government weakened, she and ailing husband Nestor Kirchner -- her predecessor in the presidency and seen as the architect of her economic strategy -- may find such controls harder to enforce.\par \par \uc2 Farmers have threatened to resume strikes and protests to demand an end to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wheat market and business leaders may be more willing to rebel against price watchdog Guillermo Moreno, the domestic commerce secretary.\par \par \uc2 "Moreno doesn't scare like he used to," said pollster and analyst Sergio Berensztein. "But for as long as Nestor Kirchner doesn't want to sacrifice short-term growth to lower inflation ... I think we'll get more of the same."\par \par \uc2 ARGENTINA-ECONOMY/INFLATION (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100213e62a000c3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
