\par\par \b \uc2 Argentine stocks, peso edge higher despite debt row\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2010\par 16:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Stocks, peso reverse early losses\par \par \uc2 * Bonds trade higher despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tension (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Jorge Otaola\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Jan 7 (Reuters) - Argentine financial markets rebounded from early losses to end with light gains on Thursday despite concern over a dispute between the president and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief over using foreign reserves to pay debt.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerVal <.MERV> stocks index closed up 1.14 percent at 2,389.145 points, reversing earlier losses on bargain hunting a day after President Cristina Fernandez asked \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Martin Redrado to resign. For details see [ID:N07183139]\par \par \uc2 Government debt traded over the counter in Buenos Aires ended up 0.2 percent on average as medium-sized investors and state-run banks bought back bonds.\par \par \uc2 Among the biggest gainers on the local debt market was peso-denominated Discount paper <ARDISCP=RASL>, sliding 1.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 Fernandez asked Redrado to step down on Wednesday after he blocked her order to use some $6.6 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to repay debt. He refused to step down, saying only Congress can remove him.\par \par \uc2 Late on Thursday, she signed a decree firing him.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso closed up 0.19 percent at 3.8625/3.8675 per U.S. dollar <ARSB=> in informal trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, as measured by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 In formal interbank trade, the peso rose 0.46 percent to close at 3.7925/3.7950 per dollar<ARS=RASL> due to \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's debt spreads widened 12 basis points to 668 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasuries, according to \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's EMBI+ <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 The cost to insure Argentina's debt with credit default swaps rose to an upfront cost of about 17.3 percent of the sum insured versus Wednesday's 15.9 percent. (With additional reporting by Sujata Rao-Coverley; Writing by Luis Andres Henao; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ARGENTINA/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100107e61700135\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
