\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Up Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Slip\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shane Romig   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2009\par 22:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar came under heavy selling pressure in Argentina Wednesday, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in to stem the appreciation of the peso.\par \par \uc2 The peso fell to 3.8000 to the dollar from 3.8050 on Monday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were closed Tuesday for a national holiday.\par \par \uc2 From the start of trade, the peso gained ground, leading the government to buy dollars to stem selling pressure.\par \par \uc2 The government regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maintain the peso in a managed float.\par \par \uc2 The peso has remained relatively stable against the dollar due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the sharp appreciation of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Argentine peso is down 10% against the dollar so far this year, while the Brazilian real has gained 24% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, stocks eased as prices were adjusted to reflect the losses posted in international markets Tuesday, when local trade was shut.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's Merval Index shed 0.47% to close at 2,162.63 points.\par \par \uc2 Falling international oil prices also pushed down the local listing of Brazil's \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (APBR), which fell 3.34% to close at ARS92.50.\par \par \uc2 Bond trade was choppy, with most prices posting small movements.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark peso-denominated bond rose 0.18% in price terms to ARS113.90, while the dollar-denominated Boden 2012 fell 0.12% in price terms to ARS324.60.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4103-6738; shane.romig@dowjones.com [ 09-12-09 2108GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020091209e5c90003o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
