\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Peso Steady After Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 17:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso declined abruptly in the first 20 minutes of trading Tuesday but quickly strengthened after the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling dollars, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "The peso fell to ARS3.64 to the U.S. dollar but strengthened to ARS3.62 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $100 million," said Francisco Diaz Mayer, a trader at ABC Mercado de Cambios.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman was not immediately available for comment.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS3.6063 Monday.\par \par \uc2 A bit later Tuesday the bank sold another $100 million and the peso moved to ARS3.61, Diaz Mayer said.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes after the peso slipped almost four centavos Monday, its fastest decline in many months, leading to speculation that the bank had decided to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slide faster and further than before.\par \par \uc2 "It's clear the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to keep the peso from moving too quickly," said Diaz Mayer. "The bank is the only seller of dollars in the market."\par \par \uc2 -By Taos Turner, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4590-2421; taos.turner@dowjones.com [ 03-03-09 1620GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090303e533000pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
