\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Bonds Dn On Fitch Rating Cut; Stocks Dn, Peso Unch\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shane Romig   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2008\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine bonds were generally lower Thursday following a downgrading of Argentina's debt by Fitch Ratings, while stocks broke an 11-day run of gains to close lower on profit-taking.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed unchanged against the dollar as strong demand from exporters seeking to turn their dollars into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was balanced by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Near the end of trade Thursday, Fitch Ratings downgraded \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issuer default rating, or IDR, local bond rating and country ceiling.\par \par \uc2 The IDR was lowered to B- from B, the performing bonds in foreign and local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  governed by Argentine law rating was lowered to B-/RR4 from B/RR4 and the country ceiling was lowered to B from B+.\par \par \uc2 "Lower economic growth, falling commodity prices and limited funding sources have increased the risk of Argentina facing difficulties in meeting significant fiscal and external financing needs over the next two years," Erich Arispe, associate director in Fitch's Latin America Sovereign Group, said in a press release Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The downgrade followed the release earlier in the day of gross domestic product numbers that indicated a slowdown in growth. The pace of Argentina's economic growth in the third quarter was up 6.5% on the year, and up 1.3% from the previous quarter, the national statistics agency INDEC said. That follows growth of more than 8% in each of the past five years.\par \par \uc2 The government also revised upward its second-quarter GDP year-on-year growth estimate to 7.6%, from 7.5% previously.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark discount bond in pesos fell 4.39% in price terms to close at ARS49 ($14.38). The discount bond is yielding 21.21%.\par \par \uc2 Stocks also closed lower as traders cashed in on gains made over the past two weeks. The Merval index of leading shares fell 2.74% to close at 1,116.43 points. Thirty-nine companies ended the day lower, 13 were unchanged and 13 rose. Volume was light at ARS57 million.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed unchanged at 3.4075 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Most of the dollar offer came from liquidating exports (and) the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying to maintain the exchange parity," Puente Hermanos brokerage said in a market note.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4590-2438; shane.romig@dowjones.com [ 18-12-08 2135GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020081218e4ci0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
