\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks get boost from oil price rise\b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2008\par 21:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Dec 10 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks got a charge on Wednesday from higher crude prices, and the peso also rose in light volume as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to reverse a long slump in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerVal index <.MERV> closed 3.33 percent higher at 1,060.87. On the broad market volume was dull at $13 million and of active issues 43 advanced, 14 declined and 12 were unchanged.\par \par \uc2 Bellwether \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  , a global leader in steel tubes for the oil industry, was the session's value leader, rising 2.3 percent to 34.8 pesos per share.\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires-listed shares of Brazilian oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  roared up 9.5 percent to 38.9 pesos per share.\par \par \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  and \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  together are weighted at close to a third of the MerVal.\par \par \uc2 "The MerVal is rising again, thanks to \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  and \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  in a rebound linked to raw materials, especially petroleum," said Claudio Szlaien, analyst with Marlon Financial Resources in Buenos Aires.\par \par \uc2 Oil rose more than 3 percent on Wednesday on signs that OPEC kingpin Saudi Arabia has slashed supplies to customers for January.\par \par \uc2 In formal trade between banks the peso gained 0.44 percent to 3.4150/3.4175 per dollar <ARS=RASL>. In trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, as measured by Reuters, jumped 0.95 percent to 3.4600/3.4650 per dollar <ARSB=>.\par \par \uc2 Traders said volume was thin and the price was guided by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pursued a policy of sustaining its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than allowing a sharp depreciation as has happened in Mexico and Brazil, but over the past three weeks the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slumped steadily.\par \par \uc2 Sovereign bond prices rose on average in over-the-counter trade in Buenos Aires, led by a 6.2 percent rise in the Boden 2012 peso-denominated bonds to an ask price of 91.2 <ARBODEN12=RASL>. (Reporting by Jorge Otaola and Walter Bianchi; Writing by Fiona Ortiz; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ARGENTINA|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081210e4ca001k9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
