\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Stks Dn, Bonds Mixed, Peso Up on Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2008\par 22:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine stocks ended the day moderately lower after rising in line with Wall Street in the morning and following it lower in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Bonds were mixed, with most closing lower on continued uncertainty, while the peso inched higher on government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Merval index of leading shares fell 0.97% to close at 1,085.87 points. The index was up as high as 3.84% in early trade and was down as much 2.75% in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The early gains were led by steel tube maker \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  (TS), which benefitted by rising oil prices, but \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  gave back some of that ground in the afternoon to close just 2.6% higher at ARS41.35 ($12.53).\par \par \uc2 BBVA Banco Frances (FRAN) ended 1.96% lower, at ARS3.50, despite reporting third-quarter net earnings at the end of trade of ARS117 million ($30 million), up 60% from ARS73 million a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 Bonds were mixed, with continued uncertainty over the country's economic prospects and amid Senate debate of the government's plan to nationalize the private pension fund system.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2012 dollar denominated bond rose 0.49% in price terms to the dollar equivalent of ARS154.50. The benchmark discount bond in pesos fell 1.59% to ARS46.50.\par \par \uc2 The House passed the nationalization bill last week and President Cristina Kirchner is pushing hard for a fast vote from the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Amid the international financial crisis, confidence is falling and Argentine private sector bank deposits fell 2.8% in October, \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  analyst Pablo Mora said in a market note.\par \par \uc2 "The government's decision to seize the private pension funds...further fueled such loss of confidence," Mora said.\par \par \uc2 "Unless confidence is restored, deposits are likely to continue falling and people are likely to continue seeking refuge in the U.S. dollar, placing continued pressure on the exchange rate," Mora said.\par \par \uc2 However, the peso gained a little ground due to government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The peso closed at ARS3.3 to the dollar, up from ARS3.305.\par \par \uc2 Volume was very low, with the exchange rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , brokerage Portfolio Personal said in a market note.\par \par \uc2 The government's "monitoring of transactions and the slowing of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases has resulted in the private demand for dollars being temporarily replaced by government activity," Portfolio Personal said.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4590-2438; shane.romig@dowjones.com [ 10-11-08 2122GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020081110e4ba0000q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
