\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso, Bonds Dn Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2008\par 22:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine stocks made late gains to pull the index into the black at the end of trade Wednesday, while bonds and the peso slipped ahead of Thursday's bank holiday, which will see markets closed. Shares moved higher in the last two minutes of trade as the government's Banco de la Nacion stepped in to buy, said a trader who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 The Merval index of leading shares rose 1.12% to close at 1,135.79 points. The index was down as much as 2.56% during the last hour of trade before late buyers stepped in.\par \par \uc2 Banco de la Nacion stepped in to buy late in the session partly to support battered share vales and partly as an investment decision, said the trader.\par \par \uc2 With the Merval down from about 2,200 points in June, some investors also did some buying to take advantage of the "extraordinarily low" share values, said Cohen Financial Services Group analyst Jaqueline Maubre.\par \par \uc2 Yet confidence remains weak due to the international financial crisis and a series of market-unfriendly decisions made by the government recently.\par \par \uc2 That lack of confidence was reflected in falling bond prices Wednesday after solid gains posted since last Friday.\par \par \uc2 The government stepped in to buy back its own debt Tuesday, purchasing ARS150 million of Boden 2012 bonds, a trader said. While the government was expected to continue its secretive buyback program, the lack of purchases on Wednesday led to sharp declines.\par \par \uc2 "No one excepts the government is interested in buying bonds right now," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The Boden 2012 dollar denominated bond fell 3.61% in price terms to the dollar equivalent of ARS156.15.\par \par \uc2 The peso also eased on Wednesday despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso closed at 3.30375 to the dollar, down from 3.29125\par \par \uc2 The Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday made the unprecedented move of forcing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange houses to overturn market transactions that had already occurred as part of its bid to steady the peso, said Hector Blanco, a trader with ABC Mercado de Cambios.\par \par \uc2 Traders say the inspections are tantamount to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls and are a roundabout way of pushing banks and exchange houses to work within certain limits.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official on Wednesday would neither confirm nor deny that it had reversed transactions. He said the bank is simply "trying to guarantee that traders are complying with new rules" issued Monday that impose a minimum three-day holding period on the purchase of stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 Investors had been buying foreign stocks and bonds here and then immediately selling them in New York, where they could deposit U.S. dollars obtained from the deal. This allowed them to get dollars quickly without having to deal with burdensome \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations in Argentina.\par \par \uc2 Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, together with officials from the Argentine Securities Exchange and the national tax agency, AFIP, have been auditing exchange houses and trader \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at banks since Monday.\par \par \uc2 Blanco said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been pushing exporters to sell their dollars in the market to alleviate pressure on the peso.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4590-2438; shane.romig@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Taos Turner contributed to this report) [ 05-11-08 2103GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020081105e4b50003m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
