\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso, Bucking Trend, Ends Up After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael Casey   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 22:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--After a dramatic last-hour rally that followed repeated heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the day, the Argentine peso reversed a big earlier slide that had been fueled by retail selling.\par \par \uc2 In the end, it closed stronger than its Thursday close, remarkably bucking another sharp fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its giant neighbor, Brazil.\par \par \uc2 At the close of interbank trading at 3 p.m. local time (1800 GMT), the peso was at ARS3.2225 to the dollar, a full centavo stronger than the ARS3.2325 level it finished with on Thursday. Earlier in the day, it weakened as far as ARS3.27 as the Brazilian real went into yet another freefall and Argentines began pulling money out of banks.\par \par \uc2 As the initial slide took hold, the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. Hector Blanco, of ABC Mercado de Cambio, estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered $539 million in total while the actual amount transacted was between $450 million and $500 million.\par \par \uc2 For most of the day, these dollar sales contained the peso's descent but did not reverse it. Then, traders said, the sudden surge came at the end and was driven not by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand for pesos but by a small number of banks seeking peso liquidity in preparation for a long holiday weekend. The five-centavo jump in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  corresponded to a mere $40-50 million in dollar sales, Blanco said.\par \par \uc2 Long lines were seen through the day at local banks, with many customers switching into dollars. This meant that in contradiction with the wholesale interbank rate, the price for dollars at the retail level ended higher on the day, with the greenback offered at ARS3.27, compared with ARS3.24 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Faced with this worrying sign, the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to demonstrate that it won't let the exchange rate be driven by external forces, Blanco said. This is in keeping with Bank President Martin Redrado's promise not to undermine stability in the banking sector.\par \par \uc2 "They want a gradual depreciation, not fast depreciations to match Brazil's," he said. However, he added that this may not be sustainable, given that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina's biggest trading partner has lost more than a quarter of its value since September amid the massive global flight to quality caused by the current financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 The weakness in the real and other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  puts the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bind.\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, it creates a competitiveness challenge at a time when Argentina must also contend with a sharp drop in the international price for its agricultural commodities. But on other hand, it cannot let the peso-dollar rate drop too far because of inflation risks and the historically important role that the exchange rate plays in the confidence of Argentine savers.\par \par \uc2 Years of past crises have led many Argentines to treat the peso-dollar rate as the single most important indicator of financial stability, regardless of what harm its strength might do to the underlying economy's capacity to generate foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings.\par \par \uc2 -By Michael Casey, Dow Jones Newswires; michael.j.casey@dowjones.com; 54-11-4590 2428 [ 10-10-08 2000GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081010e4aa000ww\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
