\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina boosts repos to curb 'unjustified' rates   \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2007\par 19:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it was stepping up its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local interbank money market to curb what it termed an "unjustified" jump in short-term rates fueled by global credit turmoil.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would offer up to 1 billion pesos ($313.2 million) on Monday of seven-day repurchase agreements, double the amount it had offered for sale at auctions during the last month.   \par \par \uc2 This measure "will inhibit unjustified increases on interest rates for loans," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 The repos offer an 11 percent fixed annual interest rate.   \par \par \uc2 Since July, Argentina's short-term interbank lending rates have surged to as high as 25 percent, a four-year record, fueled by instability in global markets, initially sparked in the United States by investments in risky U.S. mortgages.   \par \par \uc2 The interbank rates were in single digits before the volatility began.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considers that we have significantly reduced the repercussions ... of the strong volatility in world markets," the bank said.   \par \par \uc2 Instead of auctioning the repos, as it has since mid-August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that banks on Monday would be allowed to buy them in proportion to their share of deposits.   \par \par \uc2 The bank also said it would continue auctions to buy back up to 500 million pesos a day of notes and bills it had previously sold.   \par \par \uc2 In informal trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, as measured by Reuters, the Argentine peso <ARSB=> was trading 0.16 percent firmer at 3.1900/3.1925 per dollar at midday.   \par \par \uc2 It was steady though at 3.1350/3.1375 per dollar <ARS=RASL> in formal interbank trade, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /REPOS|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070917e39h001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
