\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina Bonds, Stocks Rebound; Merval Up 3%, But Peso Falls   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Serena Saitto   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2007\par 23:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Argentine stocks and bonds rebounded Wednesday after Tuesday's plunge amid Wall Street's renewed hopes for an interest rate cut by the U.S. Federal Reserve.   \par \par \uc2 The peso, however, weakened against the U.S. dollar, closing at ARS3.1675 versus ARS3.1650 Tuesday despite the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the peso is damaging investors' confidence in this market," said Hector Blanco, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with ABC Mercado de Cambio.   \par \par \uc2 Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar reserves were down Tuesday to $43.370 million from $43.56 billion Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the Merval benchmark index closed 3% higher to 2,045.67, returning above the important 2,000 psychological threshold it breached Tuesday when it dropped by 4.36%.   \par \par \uc2 Trading volumes were, however, subdued at a level of ARS85.47 million ($27 million), showing investors' continuing cautious mood.   \par \par \uc2 Among winners, shares of steel tube maker  \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  (TS) shined 4.72% higher to ARS75.40, also helped by oil price increase above $73 a barrel.   \par \par \uc2 The rebound also involved Argentine bonds. Closely watched inflation-linked Discount in peso closed at ARS112.47 with its yield at 8.43%, tighter than 8.57% of Tuesday's closing. The Par in peso closed at ARS41.2 with its yield down to 7.63% from 7.65% on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Investors are now waiting for Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's speech Friday at the Fed's annual symposium in Jackson Hole, Wyo.   \par \par \uc2 -By Serena Saitto, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3125; serena.saitto@dowjones.com [ 29-08-07 2128GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 5054   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070829e38t0017q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
