\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina bonds, stocks end higher on Fed cheer   \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2007\par 23:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 8 (Reuters) - Argentine bonds gained 2.7 percent on average and stocks rose nearly 2.0 percent on Wednesday, joining gains in other emerging markets buoyed by comments from the U.S. Federal Reserve on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The biggest mover among Argentine bonds, which were hard hit by recent global market losses, was the dollar-denominated Discount bond, which surged 4.3 percent in over-the-counter trade <AR/BONOS>.   \par \par \uc2 The Fed said on Tuesday that a housing slump should not stall U.S. economic growth, reducing market jitters about the overall health of the American economy and favoring riskier emerging markets assets along with Wall Street stocks.   \par \par \uc2 Argentine debt spreads over comparable U.S. Treasuries narrowed by a full 53 basis points to 406 basis points on  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's EMBI+ bond index <11EMJ>.   \par \par \uc2 "Institutional investors are once again taking positions in bonds and the market is tentatively becoming attractive again," a trader said. "We are seeing investors shift positions from the (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market to bonds."   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerVal stock index <.MERV> climbed 1.74 percent to 2,158.44 points, sharing in global market gains, with trade volume on the broad market at around 12 million pesos ($ million). Of active shares, 63 advanced, 20 declined, and 13 were unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 Steelmaker  \uc2 Tenaris\uc2 , the largest company on the MerVal , led the session's gains with a 4.45 percent surge to 79.85 pesos a share.   \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso firmed slightly against the U.S. dollar in midday trade.   \par \par \uc2 In informal trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, as measured by Reuters, the peso strengthened 0.08 percent to 3.1800/3.1825 pesos per dollar <ARSB=>. It traded 0.24 percent stronger at 3.1325/3.1350 in formal interbank trade <ARS=RASL>, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070808e3880021d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
