\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina stocks, bonds revive on U.S. Fed news   \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2007\par 23:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Aug 7 (Reuters) - Argentine stocks rose on Tuesday, led by market heavyweight steel tube maker  \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  , while bonds recovered slightly as investors shopped for bargains, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark MerVal index <.MERV> climbed 0.64 percent to end at 2,121.51 after two sinking sessions. Trade volume on the broad market was moderate at 79.8 million pesos ($25 million). Among active issues, 35 advanced, 32 declined and nine were unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 Tenaris\uc2  jumped 3.31 percent to close at 76.45 pesos per share.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said global markets responded favorably to the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision to keep interest rates fixed, offering some relief to risky emerging markets, but noted that inflation remained U.S. policy-makers' main concern.   \par \par \uc2 Argentine bonds crept up an average 0.5 percent in local trade, with the benchmark Par dollar-denominated bond climbing 5.0 percent <AR/BONOS> <ARPARD=RASL>.   \par \par \uc2 "We see opportunistic buys because the market has been really punished. At the same time, concerns about bonds are not disappearing, so the rebound is merely technical for now," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 More than half of Argentina's bonds are linked to inflation. Recent selling of the country's debt was linked to a global flight from emerging market risk -- but also due to doubts about the reliability of official price data.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the peso closed stable against the U.S. dollar. In informal trade between \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses, as measured by Reuters, the peso closed flat at 3.1825/3.1850 pesos per dollar <ARSB=>. It gave up 0.08 percent to 3.1400/3.1425 in formal interbank trade <ARS=RASL>, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 ARGENTINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070807e38700238\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
