\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  Peso Softens To ARS3.135/Dlr; Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2007\par 21:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--The Argentine peso softened against the dollar Wednesday despite apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The peso closed at ARS3.135 in the interbank market, weaker than ARS3.1225 Tuesday. Liquidity continued to ease, with the interbank interest, or call money, rate dropping slightly to 12.5% from 13% Tuesday. After the call money rate spiked to 28% Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began buying back Lebac notes, called off this week's note auction, and eased month-end reserve requirements.   \par \par \uc2 "The peso continued to weaken, basically on the return of worsening international conditions we have seen over the past two days," said one local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. He described volumes as strong and on par with recent sessions. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently sold dollars or coordinated their sale through other state-run banks, he added.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $44.19 billion as of Tuesday's close. Wednesday reserves data weren't immediately available.   \par \par \uc2 -By Drew Benson, Dow Jones Newswires; 5411-4311-3127; andrew.benson@dowjones.com [ 01-08-07 1912GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1833   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070801e381000yz\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0